# I05.var07 scheduled mission turnround — publication candidate

This case adds one `ChangesMissionTurnround` row at hour 25 for `BASIC-MISSION`, `TEACH-AIR-01`, and `BASE-01`, setting `DURN=1.5`. The direct accepted parent is the B04 v1.0.1 **turnround** arm, where both turnround tasks last one hour. The parent no-turnround control is separate source context. The inherited ProblemDescription still says one-hour turnrounds; that is the parent label and does not describe the child's second turnround.

The single v1.0.1 native attempt naturally completed four serial native commands and two pure checker stages with exit zero. The converter had 17 CRLF lines, Control warning #108 and System warning #126, and zero errors or notes. The first turnround remained at hours 23.5–24.5. The second started at hour 27, planned 1.5 hours, and ended with the aircraft ready at 28.5, compared with hour 28 in the accepted parent. No scheduled-change marker appeared at hour 25. These are observations of one frozen source-bound run, not a general rule for same-time scheduling or ChangesMissionTurnround.

The strict authored and export comparisons covered 211 and 374 typed cells in 33 tables each, including exact table order and key metadata. The physical log matched the frozen 115-line, 107-timed-line oracle byte for byte. The report comparator covered all 4,044 typed cells; the prospective change was limited to three SystemResults cells in [28, 28.5). The original-captured independent reader returned `GO_BOUNDED` on 25 read-only recovered files. A separate signed, receipt-bound decision now records `GO_BOUNDED_POSTRUN` for this one run. [The additive scope precision note](review/independent-postrun-scope-precision-2026-10-09.md) corrects one wording detail in the frozen signoff: native closure `error` and `step_error` are exact empty JSON strings. The underlying verdict and raw bytes are unchanged. Publication still requires custody, index, content, staged-byte, and remote gates.

The frozen v1.0.0 source proposal remains `STATIC_NO_GO`: before any package method or native run, root found that its source gate conflated 37 disk/Git role references with 35 unique paths and read a nonexistent catalog `id` field. V1.0.1 retains the exact frozen prospective business input and oracle, adds distinct source gates and run identity, and preserves the prior author freeze and root static seal as two historical roles. Later local PS5 `Get-FileHash` environment and PowerShell mode-inference failures were pre-native; their original proofs and separate recovery methods remain required history, not native result evidence.

The prelaunch manifest has 144 source roles: 40 owned source files, one inventory, 100 selected references to 98 protected originals, one Python runtime, and two v1.0.0 historical seals. The source selection includes 37 disk/Git role references over 35 distinct files, 24 accepted-parent raw originals and 24 excluded B04 v1.0.0 raw originals. The local CRLF and Git LF catalog-505 archives have different byte identities. The 39 new originals comprise 25 files in the native physical directory and 14 PURE/transport artifacts. Those, 15 zero-native preflight originals, and 25 read-only recovered copies remain host-bound for sealed replay; the accepted parent was not rerun.

`runs/`, `test-output/`, and `transport-evidence/` stay local and outside the proposed Git source set. Only the 863-byte converter log and 9,108-byte physical log are proposed as two small, separately mapped inert native raw copies under `preserved-raw/`; its allowed `custody.json` name identifies both originals and copies. The two full *derived prospective* export/report oracle files and both byte-distinct catalog-505 archives are frozen owned sources required by the prelaunch inventory and independent reader, so the proposed closed source set retains them. The frozen prelaunch README and `.gitignore` treated the two derived oracles as host-only. A separate finite source/content review supersedes that earlier publication classification: staging requires an exact reviewed allowlist with explicit force-add for precisely those two ignored fixture files. Full *native raw* SXI/SXO/export/report, accepted and failed raw, and installed manual/dictionary/executable/database remain host-bound by exact pins. The curated logs do not replace the 39 originals or the 25 recovered replay files. The final staged allowlist and evidence index require independent content review before any publication.

This candidate covers only the hour-25 scheduled change before the second turnround. It does not establish a general scheduling precedence law, every I05 variant, GUI behavior, cross-engine equivalence, performance, CI success, or Issue 18 completion.
